 ## Git and Agent Workflow
 - Do not revert or rewrite unrelated user changes.
 - Avoid destructive Git commands unless explicitly requested.
 - Before commit/PR, run relevant tests and formatting checks for touched services.
 - In commit/PR notes, mention:
   - touched service(s)
   - executed checks
   - whether Docker/Testcontainers tests were run
 - Keep this document concise and accurate; prune outdated rules when adding new ones.
+
+## MCP Tooling
+- MCP templates live in `mcp/` for Claude Desktop, Windsurf, and OpenCode.
+- Use `mcp/claude_desktop_config.json` for Claude Desktop, `mcp/windsurf_mcp_config.json` for Windsurf, and `mcp/opencode.json` for OpenCode.
+- Required code-intelligence tools are `graphify`, `java-lsp`, and `java-app-modernization`.
+- Use `graphify` first for repository-wide understanding, architecture questions, file relationships, and scoped graph queries.
+- Use `java-lsp` for Java symbol navigation, diagnostics, local refactorings, rename previews, hover/type info, and call/type hierarchy after the Java language server is available.
+- Use `java-app-modernization` only for Java/Spring upgrade, migration, and modernization analysis; keep telemetry disabled with `APPMOD_MCP_COLLECT_TELEMETRY=false`.
+- The Java LSP config is `mcp/lsp-mcp.json` and expects `jls` on `PATH`; if unavailable, fall back to graphify plus Gradle verification.
+- Data/runtime MCP servers are `bookstore-postgres-catalog`, `bookstore-postgres-order`, `bookstore-postgres-inventory`, `bookstore-redis`, and `bookstore-keycloak`.
+- Kafka inspection uses `mcp/.kafka-mcp.json` with `kafka-mcp`; Kafka MCP support is currently CLI-oriented rather than a full stdio MCP server in this repo.
 
